    {
      "id": "zpmqa5c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO VOICE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The active subject becomes the passive object, while the active object becomes the main subject in passive voice.",
        "Passive voice strictly requires the third form of the verb (Past Participle - V3) accompanied by a suitable helping verb.",
        "Intransitive verbs (verbs without a direct object) cannot be transformed into passive voice.",
        "The phrase 'by + subject' is omitted when the active agent is unknown, indefinite, or completely obvious.",
        "Imperative sentences convert to passive structures using 'Let + Object + be + V3' or advisory phrases like 'You are requested/ordered to'."
      ],
      "id": "ikwo01x"
    },
