    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gk7sx3k"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "The grammatical tense of a sentence NEVER changes during Active-Passive transformation; only the structure changes.",
        "Watch out for specific verbs that take prepositions other than 'by' in passive form (e.g., 'known to', 'surprised at', 'pleased with').",
        "Interrogative sentences starting with 'Who' change to 'By whom' in passive voice, maintaining question word order."
      ],
      "id": "r7eua0e"
